  "interpretation": "Over 696 km2 of flat farmland the median HV rose by about 1.3 dB from late June to early September (-18.6 to -17.4 dB) and HH by about 1.1 dB, consistent with crops (mainly cotton) growing taller and denser. The signal stays high through 13 Oct: cotton in Khatlon is picked by hand from September to November and the plants stay in the field, so no large harvest drop is expected yet. Only 25 km2 (3.6%) show an HV drop of 3 dB or more; treat these as candidate early-harvested or cleared fields, not a confirmed harvest map. No acquisition on 2 Aug (gap 21 Jul to 14 Aug).",
